<p>Containment procedures aren't very thorough at all, and it's pretty fucking hard to screw up freezing something and shoving it into an underground bunker. The definition that seems to be gathering momentum among the senior staff is the "containment difficulty" one, and containing 008 barely costs anything. Under the current definition it fulfills the whole "kill everybody" criteria but doesn't have the "containment protocols must be extensive, involved, and precisely followed in order to prevent it from doing so" one.</p>

