														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1182665">
									

<p>The thing is, this isn't just another virus. [pedantry] For one thing, it's a prion. [/pedantry] For another, <em>this is the SCP.</em> We wouldn't be containing these items at all if they didn't bend or outright break the laws of nature as we know them.</p>
<p>Those laws dictate that in six billion people, some resistant alleles exist, and that the disease probably wouldn't spread to rural areas. Okay. They also dictate that a human with blood viscosity so high that he hardly notices gunshot wounds cannot continue to move &#8212; his circulatory system is effectively one big useless clot. SCP-008 <em>already</em> breaks natural laws. What's to say it can't have genuine 100% lethality, or spread like wildfire even without an obvious host pool?</p>
<p>I understand where you're coming from, I really do. Browsing through this site frequently forces me to give my inner scientist a couple Valium and a nice lie-down &#8212; but I keep reading, and I have fun doing it. You shouldn't have to tell your disbelief to go suck it, but the willingness to suspend it a little bit in the right places is what makes the SCP work.</p>

							</div>

