			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1182690">
									

<p>Also, there is a virus that, so far as we know, has 100% lethality. It's a genetically modified mousepox virus. Scientists altered a gene, hoping to induce sterility in mice. It killed every single mouse that was infected. They had <em>no</em> defense against it. As mousepox is extremely similar to smallpox, this is of obvious concern.</p>
<p>So, yeah, while there's resistance to most diseases we know of, it is not the hard and fast rule we once thought it was.</p>

