														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1183490">
									

<p>Well, I see what the pro-article people are saying about suspension of disbelief, I accept 100% contagion as an artifact of the eldritch gods. But the problem with zombies is that they are shit. They move slow, and have to catch someone to transmit the virus. But they also eat people, so they are crap at creating zombies, because many of the zombies they create are not functional.</p>
<p>So we have a disease that can only be transmitted to people who are unlucky enough to cross paths with a zombie, get bitten AND escape their attackers reasonably in tact. It would cause all hell to break loose in the first city it hit, then would be contained within a few days.</p>
<p>The only way to make scary zombies dangerous is to make them fast and non-decomposing (28 days later) or change the method of contagion (The Cell) or both (Quatermass).</p>

